 # queue-lost-retry
 
 A compact stateful single-job queue project. Run `npm test` with Node 24 or newer.
+
+`queue(jobs)` stores ready jobs and tracks the one job currently being worked.
+`work(q, send)` takes one job and calls `send(job)` once. A truthy result marks
+the job delivered and removes it. A falsy result returns the job, including its
+ID and payload, to ready work without leaving a lease; other ready jobs remain
+available. A later call can successfully consume that retried job.
+
+When there is no ready job, `work` returns `{sent: [], retried: []}` and does
+not call `send`.
+
+The regression suite covers successful delivery, failed delivery followed by a
+retry while preserving unrelated work, and idle processing of an empty queue.
